{"Accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a TypeError when `evt.destinationCalendar` is empty or null, as `mainHostDestinationCalendar` becomes `undefined`. Use optional chaining (`mainHostDestinationCalendar?.integration`) to prevent a runtime crash.": 0.952033281326294, "The condition was inverted: when team billing is **disabled**, `slug` is now omitted, which can create organizations without a slug. That breaks subdomain routing and any lookups relying on `team.slug`. Restore the previous condition so non-team-billing orgs always get a slug.": 0.8829300403594971, "createEvent (line 85): Adding a required `credentialId` parameter breaks the `Calendar` interface contract. This will cause compilation errors and runtime failures (incorrectly defaulting to the 'primary' calendar) unless the interface in `@calcom/types/Calendar` and all call sites are updated to provide this ID.": 0.17027275264263153, "This change clears `credentialId` for non-calendar (video) references. This is inconsistent with `updateLocation` and breaks flows that rely on the specific credential ID stored in the reference (e.g., identifying the correct account for updates when multiple are connected). Use `credentialId: result.credentialId` for all results.": 0.4786573648452759, "This database lookup pulls a credential by raw ID without verifying ownership, bypassing the security context established in the constructor. This introduces an IDOR vulnerability where a manipulated `destinationCalendar` entry allows operations on another user's calendar. Constrain the query to the `userId` or `teamId` associated with the current `EventManager` context.": 0.5422637462615967, "When `externalCalendarId` is falsy, this `find` compares against the same falsy value, so it will almost always return `undefined`, yielding an invalid `calendarId` for the update call. Use a real fallback (e.g., first destination calendar or `primary`) instead of matching on an absent ID.": 0.9874690771102905, "The `teamDestinationCalendars` collected here will be silently discarded if the organizer lacks a destination calendar. In the `evt` object initialization (line 1088), `destinationCalendar` is set to `null` if no organizer calendar is found. Consequently, the optional chaining at line 1101 (`evt.destinationCalendar?.push`) does nothing. Initialize `evt.destinationCalendar` to an empty array `[]` instead of `null` to ensure team calendars are correctly included in collective bookings.": 0.9850136637687683}